# CODEOWNERS — intentionally declares NO owned paths.
#
# Branch protection still has "Require review from Code Owners" switched on, and
# `gate` is still a required status check. This file simply declares nothing as
# owned, so the code-owner rule has nothing to require. The protection mechanism
# stays intact and switching it back on is a matter of uncommenting lines below.
#
# Why: on 2026-09-13 Tom removed the approval requirement entirely — Claude merges
# anything that passes the quality gate, user-facing included (see CLAUDE.md). The
# ownership entries below were the actual enforcement of the old rule. The
# review-guard workflow was only a second layer; this was the one that blocked.
#
# What replaces it is not nothing, but it is not a gate either: the guard still
# classifies every PR as user-facing or internal and labels it, user-facing merges
# get reported to Tom afterwards, and anything touching money, legal text,
# unrecoverable data or a product direction still escalates to him by judgement
# rather than by mechanism.
#
# To restore the old boundary, uncomment any subset of these:
